            {
              "text": "For mid-market businesses in Hobart seeking consulting focused specifically on **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **AI agents**, and **practical workflow automation**, options range from specialized boutique consultancies to established regional IT providers:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Copilot Studio & Agentic AI Specialists\n\n* **FutureAbility**\n  * **Location:** Hobart-based (with local delivery in Hobart and Australia-wide support).\n  * **Focus:** FutureAbility is specifically focused on **Microsoft Copilot Studio, Power Platform, and AI agents** built directly inside a client’s Microsoft 365 tenant for **mid-market organizations**.\n  * **Why them:** They deliver official Microsoft *“Agent in a Day”* workshops and focus on taking AI beyond simple chat assistants into end-to-end, multi-agent business process automation (triage, document reading, cross-system orchestration, and replacing spreadsheet/email manual handoffs). They do not clip tickets on Microsoft licenses, focusing purely on delivery, adoption, and tenant-based IP.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Established Tasmanian Managed IT & Enterprise Partners\n\n* **Intuit Technologies**\n  * **Location:** Hobart (headquartered in Tasmania, with statewide coverage).\n  * **Focus:** One of Tasmania’s largest and most established Microsoft Cloud and IT services providers. \n  * **Capabilities:** Has dedicated practices in **Power Platform, Dynamics 365, and AI/Intelligent Automation**, actively implementing Copilot Studio and Power Automate workflows to connect CRM/ERP data with front-line business operations.\n  * **Best for:** Mid-market organizations that want broader infrastructure, cybersecurity, and managed IT services integrated with their AI automation rollouts.\n\n* **Frontrow Technology**\n  * **Location:** Hobart & Tasmania (remote-first with on-site availability).\n  * **Focus:** Microsoft Solutions Partner specializing in Microsoft 365 Copilot readiness, licensing setup, deployment, and practical organizational adoption. \n\n* **IT Strategic**\n  * **Location:** Hobart & Melbourne.\n  * **Focus:** IT advisory and transformation consultancy assisting SMEs, mid-market businesses, and not-for-profits with Microsoft Copilot integration, Power Platform automations, data security, and governance.\n\n* **Cyberhaven Technologies**\n  * **Location:** Hobart City.\n  * **Focus:** IT and cyber security firm offering guidance and integration support around Microsoft 365 Copilot and business automation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. National Consultancies Active in Hobart\n\n* **Rapid Circle**\n  * **Profile:** A tier-one Microsoft Solutions Partner that regularly hosts executive roundtables, modern work briefings, and agentic AI workshops in Hobart (often partnering with local groups like TasICT).\n  * **Capabilities:** Deep expertise in enterprise-grade Copilot Studio development, Power Platform Center of Excellence (CoE), custom Copilot agents, and Azure OpenAI integration.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions for Mid-Market Businesses Evaluating Providers\n\nWhen vetting a consultant for Copilot Studio and AI agents, ask them to clarify:\n1. **In-Tenant Architecture:** Do they build agents directly inside your Microsoft Dataverse/Power Platform environment so you retain total ownership of the intellectual property?\n2. **Data Governance & Permissions:** Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Studio index data based on existing user permissions; ensure the consultant includes an access-permission and data-hygiene audit prior to deployment.\n3. **Agent Scope:** Look for partners who prioritize *deterministic workflows* (rule-based handoffs in Power Automate) alongside *probabilistic agents* (Copilot Studio), rather than relying purely on generic conversational chat.",
